#: ../../source/pseudomap_README.md:1
msgid "pseudomap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pseudomap_README.md:3
msgid ""
"A thing that is a lot like ES6 `Map`, but without iterators, for use in "
"environments where `for..of` syntax and `Map` are not available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pseudomap_README.md:6
msgid ""
"If you need iterators, or just in general a more faithful polyfill to ES6"
" Maps, check out [es6-map](http://npm.im/es6-map)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pseudomap_README.md:9
msgid ""
"If you are in an environment where `Map` is supported, then that will be "
"returned instead, unless `process.env.TEST_PSEUDOMAP` is set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pseudomap_README.md:12
msgid ""
"You can use any value as keys, and any value as data.  Setting again with"
" the identical key will overwrite the previous value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pseudomap_README.md:15
msgid ""
"Internally, data is stored on an `Object.create(null)` style object. The "
"key is coerced to a string to generate the key on the internal data-bag "
"object.  The original key used is stored along with the data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pseudomap_README.md:19
msgid ""
"In the event of a stringified-key collision, a new key is generated by "
"appending an increasing number to the stringified-key until finding "
"either the intended key or an empty spot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pseudomap_README.md:23
msgid ""
"Note that because object traversal order of plain objects is not "
"guaranteed to be identical to insertion order, the insertion order "
"guarantee of `Map.prototype.forEach` is not guaranteed in this "
"implementation.  However, in all versions of Node.js and V8 where this "
"module works, `forEach` does traverse data in insertion order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pseudomap_README.md:29
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pseudomap_README.md:31
msgid ""
"Most of the [Map API](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-"
"US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Map), with the following "
"exceptions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pseudomap_README.md:35
msgid "A `Map` object is not an iterator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pseudomap_README.md:36
msgid ""
"`values`, `keys`, and `entries` methods are not implemented, because they"
" return iterators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pseudomap_README.md:38
msgid ""
"The argument to the constructor can be an Array of `[key, value]` pairs, "
"or a `Map` or `PseudoMap` object.  But, since iterators aren't used, "
"passing any plain-old iterator won't initialize the map properly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pseudomap_README.md:43
msgid "USAGE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pseudomap_README.md:45
msgid "Use just like a regular ES6 Map."
msgstr ""

